## Analytics Implementation Details

According to the fetched Vercel documentation, the implementation follows the correct pattern for Next.js App Router:

```typescript
// src/app/layout.tsx
import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html lang="es">
      <body>
        {children}
        <Analytics />  // ✅ Correctly placed
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## How to Enable Web Analytics

The code is correctly configured. To activate tracking:

1. Deploy this code to Vercel (already done in previous deployment)
2. Navigate to your project's Analytics tab in the Vercel dashboard
3. Click "Enable Web Analytics" if not already enabled
4. Analytics will automatically collect:
   - Page views
   - Web Vitals (LCP, FID, CLS, TTFB, INP)
   - Device and browser information
   - Geographic data

